  make -n on the variant directories schedules floorplan first, no
  synthesis step.

  Macro halo: no script of this ORFS version reads MACRO_PLACE_HALO,
  and rtl_macro_placer gets no halo option; it keeps half of the
  minimum macro channel (RTLMP_MIN_CHANNEL_SIZE, platform default
  "80 80") around each macro. Check (floorplan + macro placement only,
  FLOW_VARIANT=halochk): RTLMP_MIN_CHANNEL_SIZE="40 40" gives
  `rtl_macro_placer ... -min_channel_size "40 40"` and "Area of macros
  with halos: 3295023.54" = the 7 OpenRAM macros (LEF sizes) plus 20 um
  on each side; "80 80" gives 3698426.94 = plus 40 um, which is what
  every CPU run above used (also the "20 um-halo" v2/10 run). The CPU
  block config now sets RTLMP_MIN_CHANNEL_SIZE ?= 80 80 (40 um halos,
  the setting of the clean 11.22 mm^2 sizing run) instead of the
  unread MACRO_PLACE_HALO; both variant logs show -min_channel_size
  "80 80" and 3698426.94.

